      "message": "I suppose this might be safe if the intervening statement has no references to the current `fUninitializedVarDecl`. Is that case worth detecting?\n\nI suppose one could also apply this optimization to a program like this:\n\n    int a;\n    int b;\n    int c, d;\n    a \u003d 1;\n    b \u003d 2;\n    c \u003d 3;\n    d \u003d c;\n    \nDo you think that\u0027s worth exploring in a future CL?",
